tasks.body:
**Files:** create `pkgs/evidence/report.py`, `tests/evidence/test_report.py`, `tests/evidence/fixtures/report/` (a store with a `plans.jsonl` of six judgements and a fixture repo with reviews and a ledger); modify `pkgs/evidence/evidence.py` (dispatch `report` to the sibling module), `docs/runbooks/evidence.md` (the report's four lines and its n-gate).

**Interfaces:**
- `python3 pkgs/evidence/evidence.py [--store S] report plans --repo <path> [--today YYYY-MM-DD] [--min-n 5]`. Reads: `plans` rows (P6) from the store; the repo's graph through `tasks.build`-equivalent pieces — `read_reviews`, `parse_plan` over `docs/superpowers/plans/*.md`, `chain_root`, and `docs/ledger/plan-defects.toml` (P3A). Prints, each line with its n:
  1. `first-try landing rate: <a>/<n> chains (<pct>%)` — a chain is a root key that has at least one review among its members; first-try = the root's own review is `APPROVED`; `n` = chains gated; per plan when `--plan` is given, else over every typed plan;
  2. `plan-caused share of rejections: <m>/<r> (<pct>%)` — from the ledger plus blocks, `plan_defect` primary in the four plan classes over all rejection rows;
  3. `re-plan rate: <k>/<n> chains` — chains with a member whose suffix contains `r`;
  4. `rework rounds per landed task: <rounds>/<landed> = <x.xx>` — rounds = members beyond the root across landed chains;
  5. `rubric score before dispatch: n=<j>` then per judged plan `<plan> total <t> decision <d> first-try <a>/<n>` joined by plan file name (`plans.plan` basename = the task's `plan`), and `survivors outside the named set: <sum of mutants_outside_named>/<gates with the field>` or `unmeasured (no review carries mutants_outside_named)`; `operator interventions per plan: unmeasured`;
  6. after ten judged plans with `decision: dispatch`: `threshold proposal: <score>` = the lowest total among dispatched plans whose first-try rate ≥ 70%, or `no score separates ≥ 70% first-try plans yet`.
  The n-gate: lines 1–4 print only when `n ≥ --min-n` (default 5), else `refused: n=<n> < 5 (no conclusion under five)`; line 5 prints its own n and the join only when `j ≥ 5`, else `rubric score before dispatch: n=<j>, refused`; line 6 only when `j ≥ 10`. Exit 0 always except an unreadable store or repo (exit 2 with a message). Every number is a proxy for the design §7 goal it stands in for; the report's header line says so: `# evidence report plans — proxies for docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-05-planning-agent-design.md §7; n printed with every figure`.
- When telemetry T10a/T10b land, this report's join moves onto their reader layer; the output lines stay.

**Facts (planning time):** the corpus numbers the report must reproduce on this tree (design §7 "today" column): first-try 28/58 = 48%, plan-caused 42/59 = 71%, re-plan 11/58 = 19%, rework 30/58 ≈ 0.52 — with the caveat that the ledger seeds 48 rows (P3A), so line 2 on this tree prints `45/48` until the orchestrator adds the 14 unlisted rows (Dispatch); lines 1, 3, 4 come from the reviews and plans alone and must match 28/58, 11/58, 30/58 when computed over the ten typed 2026-09-05 plans (`ls docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-05-*.md`) — the chain-counting rule above is the one the design's tally used; if the live numbers differ, the report prints what the rule yields and the commit body states the difference with the chains that account for it (a wrong fact in the design is reported, never routed around).

- [ ] **Step 1: Tests, red on main** (pytest): (1) the fixture repo of six chains (two first-try, two one-fix-round, one re-plan, one open) and a store of six judgements (five `dispatch`, one `revise`) → the four lines with `2/5`, `1/5`, `3/4 = 0.75`… computed by hand in the test and asserted byte-exact (mutant: count a `b` member as a re-plan → line 3 changes → fails; mutant: count the open chain → n = 6 → fails); (2) `--min-n 5` with four chains → `refused: n=4 < 5` and no line 1 (mutant: lower the gate to 2 → the refusal fixture prints → fails — the design's mutant); (3) a store with one judgement → `rubric score before dispatch: n=1, refused`; with five → the join prints one line per plan, the plan without tasks in the repo prints `first-try —/0`; (4) ten dispatched judgements, four plans at 100% first-try with totals 36, 38, 35, 41 and six under → `threshold proposal: 35` (mutant: `max` instead of `min` → 41 → fails); nine → no proposal line; (5) `mutants_outside_named` present on two of four fixture reviews → `<sum>/2`; absent everywhere → `unmeasured …`; (6) `--plan` restricts line 1 to that plan's chains. Red: `nix develop -c pytest tests/evidence/test_report.py -q` → `ModuleNotFoundError: report`.
- [ ] **Step 2: Implement.** **Step 3: Green** — ruff; `nix develop -c pytest tests/evidence -q`; `nix build .#checks.x86_64-linux.evidence-unit -L --no-link`; lint gate; live: `nix develop -c python3 pkgs/evidence/evidence.py --store /nonexistent report plans --repo .` on this tree — paste all lines (the store is absent, so line 5 refuses; lines 1–4 print the corpus). **Step 4: One commit.**
